---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
const title = 'Privacy Policy | Proof to Partner';
const description = 'Learn what information Proof to Partner collects through its enquiry form, how it is used and stored, and how to request access or deletion.';
const breadcrumbs = [{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy policy', path: '/privacy/' }];
---
<SiteLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/privacy/" breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}>
<section class="border-b border-line bg-white py-14 sm:py-20"><div class="container-shell max-w-4xl"><p class="eyebrow">Privacy and information</p><h1 class="display-heading mt-5 text-5xl font-semibold sm:text-6xl">Privacy Policy</h1><p class="mt-5 text-sm text-muted">Last updated: 22 October 2026</p><p class="prose-copy mt-7 text-lg">This draft explains how the Proof to Partner website is designed to process business enquiries. Some operational settings still need to be confirmed before launch; see the owner review note below.</p></div></section>
<section class="section-space"><article class="container-shell max-w-4xl space-y-10">
<aside class="review-note"><h2 class="font-bold">Site owner review required before launch</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6">Confirm the operator's legal identity and location, monitored privacy contact route, retention period, data-processing jurisdictions and applicable legal obligations. This draft is not legal advice. The practices described must match the deployed settings.</p></aside>
<section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">1. Who operates this website?</h2><p class="prose-copy mt-3">The website is presented as Proof to Partner. The individual or legal entity responsible for the business, its official registered name and contact details have not been supplied for this draft. Complete those details before launch.</p></section>
<section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">2. Information collected</h2><p class="prose-copy mt-3">The enquiry form may collect your name, work email, company or organisation, website, location or coverage, product or service category, timing, message and consent confirmation. The server also processes routine request metadata needed to operate and protect the endpoint. If salted rate limiting is configured, a one-way hash derived from the request IP address is stored for abuse prevention; the raw IP is not intentionally stored in the inquiry table.</p></section>
<section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">3. How information is used</h2><ul class="prose-copy mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6"><li>To receive, store, review and respond to your enquiry.</li><li>To understand a stated commercial requirement or supplier capability.</li><li>To assess whether further discussion or a relevant introduction may be appropriate.</li><li>To limit spam and abuse, maintain the service and investigate technical errors.</li><li>To notify the configured business inbox and, if enabled, send an acknowledgement to the email address supplied.</li></ul><p class="prose-copy mt-3">Submitting an enquiry does not authorise automatic distribution of your details to prospective counterparties. Any proposed sharing should be discussed with you first.</p></section>
<section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">4. Storage and service providers</h2><p class="prose-copy mt-3">Enquiries are designed to be stored in a Cloudflare D1 database bound to a Cloudflare Worker. If email delivery is configured, the message content needed for delivery is also processed by Resend. If Cloudflare Turnstile is enabled, the browser token is verified with Cloudflare's Siteverify service. Review providers' current terms, data-processing terms and data-location settings before launch.</p></section>
<section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">5. Email and acknowledgement</h2><p class="prose-copy mt-3">Saving an enquiry to the database happens before email delivery is attempted. Notification email is sent only when valid Resend credentials, an authorised sender and a destination inbox are configured. A visitor acknowledgement is attempted only when explicitly enabled. A saved enquiry is not proof that a human has read it; the operator must monitor the inbox and database.</p></section>
<section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">6. Retention</h2><p class="prose-copy mt-3">The proposed operational target is to retain enquiry records for no longer than 12 months after the last meaningful communication, unless a longer period is reasonably needed for an ongoing business matter or legal obligation. The initial implementation does not automatically delete old records. Until automated retention is implemented, the operator must review and delete records manually. Confirm and publish the actual retention period before launch.</p></section>
<section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">7. Your choices and privacy requests</h2><p class="prose-copy mt-3">Depending on the laws that apply, you may have rights to request access, correction, deletion, restriction or objection, or to withdraw consent where consent is the relevant basis. To make a request, use the <a class="font-semibold text-brand-deep underline" href="/contact/">contact form</a>, choose General contact and identify it as a privacy request. The operator must ensure notifications and access to stored enquiries are monitored before relying on this process.</p></section>
<section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">8. Security</h2><p class="prose-copy mt-3">The implementation uses server-side validation, field and request-size limits, a honeypot, optional Turnstile verification and optional hashed-IP rate limiting. No system can guarantee absolute security. Keep account access restricted, configure secrets through Cloudflare's secret manager and avoid including sensitive information in enquiries.</p></section>
<section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">9. Cookies, analytics and external links</h2><p class="prose-copy mt-3">The initial version does not intentionally deploy advertising cookies, analytics trackers or behavioural advertising. The optional Turnstile challenge loads a third-party script when configured. External websites linked from this site have their own policies.</p></section>
<section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">10. Changes</h2><p class="prose-copy mt-3">This policy may be updated when data practices or legal requirements change. Update the date above when a substantive revision is published.</p></section>
</article></section>
</SiteLayout>